                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "457249a8-899a-3c0e-980a-7b7538d27385",
                        "entry_id": "ca737801-b192-3e6a-8499-1a5a2a9f65b6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн., устар. лицо, подготовившее условия для деятельности других лиц или для появления других событий"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c2ac6700-7fc7-4d37-8181-216d3fd1ae22",
                                "sense_id": "457249a8-899a-3c0e-980a-7b7538d27385",
                                "text": "Святая Равноапостольная Ольга, великая княгиня Российская, стала предтечей Христианства на Руси."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7bf054e9-1f9f-384c-8d6f-772d819aa32f",
                        "entry_id": "ca737801-b192-3e6a-8499-1a5a2a9f65b6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. то, что предшествует чему-либо, служит предвестием чего-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "64ff5ac5-c536-490a-bfa6-008f53fd1ff3",
                                "sense_id": "7bf054e9-1f9f-384c-8d6f-772d819aa32f",
                                "text": "Разработка сети с пакетной коммутацией Arpanet, ставшей предтечей Internet."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7605c4dd-aeba-439e-a4aa-26959c9cbf22",
                        "source_entry_id": "ca737801-b192-3e6a-8499-1a5a2a9f65b6",
                        "target_lang_word": "forerunner",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "forerunner",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe7fb0c0-ba0f-3faf-ac3f-f0e2c626da59",
                                        "entry_id": "f5127ffd-89f8-3bcf-8279-f53e29e4bd57",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A runner at the front or ahead."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5505719a-d6fb-3d9c-b3cc-02a93602657d",
                                        "entry_id": "f5127ffd-89f8-3bcf-8279-f53e29e4bd57",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "By extension, a non-competitor who leads out the competitors on to the circuit, or who runs/rides the course prior to competitor trials, usually testing or checking the way."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d82d217f-79e2-3ade-92ab-1f9966d83f78",
                                        "entry_id": "f5127ffd-89f8-3bcf-8279-f53e29e4bd57",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A precursor or harbinger, a warning ahead."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f320dee8-3225-4a25-a793-da8149ecd849",
                                                "sense_id": "d82d217f-79e2-3ade-92ab-1f9966d83f78",
                                                "text": "How meek and shrunken did that haughty Tarmac become as it slunk by the wide circle of asphalt of the yellow sort, that was loosely strewn before the great iron gates of Lady Hall as a forerunner of the consideration that awaited the guests of Rupert, Earl of Kare, […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "842a4f0c-445d-452b-a83c-8f837d6136e6",
                                                "sense_id": "d82d217f-79e2-3ade-92ab-1f9966d83f78",
                                                "text": "Acute infections of the female urethra, which are the forerunners of chronic infections, may be initiated by a number of conditions: Traumatism due to difficult labor, presence of foreign bodies such as calculi, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45127506-09d4-425d-b55c-a8bd3bcd21d2",
                                                "sense_id": "d82d217f-79e2-3ade-92ab-1f9966d83f78",
                                                "text": "On December 22, 1974, a swarm of earthquakes, the largest event being of magnitude 4.8, occurred 70 km northeast of Haicheng. All these phenomena were considered the forerunners of the major event. Thus, in January 1975, another SSB conference offered a short-term prediction that an earthquake of magnitude 5.5–6 would occur in the Yingkou-Luda-Tantung area in the first six months of 1975 (HESD, 1977)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac9594bc-91ca-33fe-9722-2a6b58fe5b7f",
                                        "entry_id": "f5127ffd-89f8-3bcf-8279-f53e29e4bd57",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A forebear, an ancestor, a predecessor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2aa0c8b-8b86-446d-a7a3-3ffab4032227",
                                                "sense_id": "ac9594bc-91ca-33fe-9722-2a6b58fe5b7f",
                                                "text": "Bakelite is a forerunner of today's plastics."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f54ddd51-b449-44ad-8c95-10f761a0093e",
                                                "sense_id": "ac9594bc-91ca-33fe-9722-2a6b58fe5b7f",
                                                "text": "The cathedral is part of the Episcopal Church, the American branch of Anglicanism. Considered the \"church of the establishment\" for much of American history -- 11 US presidents have been Episcopalian -- the church of late has been known as a forerunner of progressive theology."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4a19fdc-9e99-4efb-ab5a-4ca40c300c3b",
                                                "sense_id": "ac9594bc-91ca-33fe-9722-2a6b58fe5b7f",
                                                "text": "The result is essentially a hybrid species similar in appearance to its extinct forerunner. […] The debate over whether the wolves are a carbon copy of their extinct forerunners misses the point, Shapiro said, adding that the team had been successful in resurrecting the “functional essence” of the dire wolf."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9b46f89b-a417-3600-80ba-565b8f541d6e",
                                        "entry_id": "f5127ffd-89f8-3bcf-8279-f53e29e4bd57",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A postage stamp used in the time before a region or area issues stamps of its own."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6e669689-de0f-437d-ace9-8b6596ccbc09",
                        "source_entry_id": "ca737801-b192-3e6a-8499-1a5a2a9f65b6",
